#PAGINA LAYER
#String text
Colors cave walls by cave-in risk from dust you saw while mining (same rules as $b{Cavedust}): $col[32,220,80]{green} = safe to mine, $col[240,32,100]{red} = collapse tile, $col[255,140,32]{orange} = not yet known. Numbers on mined tiles are neighbor cave-in counts ($b{0} = all eight neighbors are safe).\n\nActivate this to show or hide the overlay. $b{$col[255,128,0]{CTRL}+activate} toggles the colored fills (numbers and ×/·/? markers stay). Importing a shared minesweeper file turns the overlay and colors on.\n\nHolding $b{$col[255,128,0]{SHIFT}} while activating this will turn on minesweeper cursor:\n• $col[255,128,0]{Clicking} will add 'danger' [$font[monospaced,10]{$col[240,32,100]{$b{×}}}] marker on the tile.\n• $col[255,128,0]{ALT+Click} will add 'safe' [$font[monospaced,10]{$col[32,220,80]{$b{·}}}] marker to the tile.\n• $col[255,128,0]{SHIFT+Click} will add 'maybe' [$font[monospaced,10]{$col[193,87,251]{$b{?}}}] to the tile.\n• $col[255,128,0]{CTRL+Click} will remove marker from the tile.\n\nThese markers can be placed on tiles with numbers, if needed.
